# Disable ALL postinstall scripts during install.
#
# Why: Hostinger's prebuild-install mirror occasionally serves stale binaries
# for esbuild (e.g. expected 0.25.12 but got 0.27.7), causing the strict
# `validateBinaryVersion` check in esbuild's install.js to throw. This fails
# the entire `npm install` even though astro build doesn't use esbuild at
# build time (esbuild is only a transitive dep of tsx, which is itself only
# needed for the `embed` + `seed-admin` scripts — not for the build).
#
# Trade-offs:
# - better-sqlite3's prebuilt `.node` binding won't be downloaded by `npm install`.
#   We rebuild it explicitly in `scripts.postinstall` below.
# - Other native modules (@node-rs/argon2, esbuild) won't fetch their prebuilts
#   during install, but they're either pure-JS bindings (@node-rs/argon2 uses
#   N-API and works without postinstall) or unused at build time (esbuild).
#
# This is the smallest, most reliable way to keep `npm install` exit-0 on
# Hostinger's flaky prebuild mirror.
ignore-scripts=true